## URL Management

### Centralized URL Configuration

Create a centralized configuration for all external URLs:

```tsx
// src/constants/urls.ts
export const EXTERNAL_URLS = {
  TERMS_OF_SERVICE: 'https://royalcanin.com/terms-of-service',
  PRIVACY_POLICY: 'https://royalcanin.com/privacy-policy',
  SUPPORT: 'https://royalcanin.com/support',
  FAQ: 'https://royalcanin.com/faq',
} as const
```

### Environment-Specific URLs

Handle different URLs for different environments:

```tsx
// src/constants/urls.ts
const getBaseURL = () => {
  if (__DEV__) {
    return 'https://staging.royalcanin.com'
  }
  return 'https://royalcanin.com'
}

export const EXTERNAL_URLS = {
  TERMS_OF_SERVICE: `${getBaseURL()}/terms-of-service`,
  PRIVACY_POLICY: `${getBaseURL()}/privacy-policy`,
} as const
```

## Accessibility and UX

### Link Styling

Use consistent styling to indicate clickable links:

```typescript
linkText: {
  fontFamily: fonts.medium,
  fontSize: fontSizes.span,
  lineHeight: lineHeights.span,
  color: theme.colors.info,
  textDecorationLine: 'underline',
},
```

### Loading States

Show loading feedback for slow-loading links:

```tsx
const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(false)

const handleLinkWithLoading = useCallback(async (url: string) => {
  setIsLoading(true)
  try {
    await Linking.openURL(url)
  } catch (error) {
    Alert.alert('Error', 'Unable to open link')
  } finally {
    setIsLoading(false)
  }
}, [])
```

## Error Handling Patterns

### Custom Error Messages

Provide specific error messages for different link types:

```tsx
const ERROR_MESSAGES = {
  TERMS: getString('auth.term'),
  PRIVACY: getString('auth.privacy'),
  SUPPORT: getString('auth.support'),
  GENERAL: getString('auth.general'),
} as const

const handleTypedLinkPress = useCallback((url: string, type: keyof typeof ERROR_MESSAGES) => {
  Linking.openURL(url).catch(() => {
    Alert.alert('Error', ERROR_MESSAGES[type])
  })
}, [])
```

### Fallback Options

Provide fallback options when links fail:

```tsx
const handleLinkWithFallback = useCallback((url: string, fallbackAction?: () => void) => {
  Linking.openURL(url).catch(() => {
    Alert.alert(getString('auth.alert_fallback'), [
      { text: getString('button.cancel'), style: 'cancel' },
      { text: getString('button.try_alternative'), onPress: fallbackAction },
    ])
  })
}, [])
```

## Platform-Specific Considerations

### iOS Deep Linking

Handle iOS-specific URL schemes:

```tsx
const handleiOSSpecificLink = useCallback((url: string) => {
  if (Platform.OS === 'ios') {
    // iOS-specific handling
    Linking.canOpenURL(url).then(supported => {
      if (supported) {
        Linking.openURL(url)
      } else {
        Alert.alert('Error', getString('error'))
      }
    })
  } else {
    // Android fallback
    Linking.openURL(url).catch(() => {
      Alert.alert('Error', getString('error'))
    })
  }
}, [])
```

### Android Intent Handling

Handle Android-specific intents when needed:

```tsx
const handleAndroidIntent = useCallback((url: string) => {
  if (Platform.OS === 'android') {
    // Android-specific handling
    Linking.openURL(url).catch(() => {
      Alert.alert('Error', getString('error'))
    })
  }
}, [])
```

## Security Considerations

### URL Sanitization

Always validate and sanitize URLs:

```tsx
const sanitizeURL = (url: string): string => {
  // Remove potentially dangerous protocols
  const dangerous = ['javascript:', 'data:', 'vbscript:']
  const lowerUrl = url.toLowerCase()

  if (dangerous.some(protocol => lowerUrl.startsWith(protocol))) {
    throw new Error(getString('error'))
  }

  return url
}
```

### Whitelist Approach

Use a whitelist for allowed domains:

```tsx
const ALLOWED_DOMAINS = ['royalcanin.com', 'support.royalcanin.com', 'help.royalcanin.com'] as const

const isAllowedDomain = (url: string): boolean => {
  try {
    const domain = new URL(url).hostname
    return ALLOWED_DOMAINS.some(allowed => domain.endsWith(allowed))
  } catch {
    return false
  }
}
```

## Testing Patterns

### Mock Linking for Tests

Mock the Linking module in tests:

```tsx
// In test files
jest.mock('react-native', () => ({
  ...jest.requireActual('react-native'),
  Linking: {
    openURL: jest.fn().mockResolvedValue(true),
    canOpenURL: jest.fn().mockResolvedValue(true),
  },
}))
```

